:: reading.paint.start.evening
{=

The makeshift curtain has ($funcReveal: "gone cold.", "dark") It shudders at your touch.

|dark)[
<br>
Though it is dark outside, your mind is alight. You close your eyes and ($funcReveal: "see...", "see")]

|see)[(either:
    [` `the Sun's ($funcReveal: "twin sister", "there") - red, rippling, and roiling beneath the surface of an obsidian lake.],
    [` `a red ($funcReveal: "slit", "there") in space, where the air peels to reveal what lies dreaming behind all things.],
    [` `violet ($funcReveal: "rays", "there") pulsating across the blackness of your lids, tracing the path with which the stars hurl through the void.],
)]

|there)[
<br>
There it is. All the hidden creatures have ($funcReveal: "come out to play.", "nurse")
]

|nurse)[
<br>
Absent the true Sun, it will have to latch onto your mind and nurse from that far light, that dwindling warmth.
(t8n: "dissolve")(show:?work)
]

|work)[
<br>
Your Work has always been performed when the world sleeps. No-one will see. No-one will know.
<br>
$cssDesc[No time like now.]

(t8n: "dissolve")(show:?mainDone)
]


:: done.paint.start.evening
{=

<!--reveal an extra paragraph if you've already read everything-->
(if: $story's lock contains "reading.painting1.evening")[(show: ?work)]

<!--choices-->
<ol>

<li>
<!--setup-->
(set: _baseChance to 50)
(set: _factorList to (passage: "table.chanceMod")'s paintStart)
|=
($funcLuckGate: "Lift up the veil.", ($funcChance: _baseChance, _factorList), [{
    <!--lock-->
    ($funcLock: "reading.painting1.evening")
}], "paint.pickApproach", "paint.failToStart")
=|
($funcChanceReadout: _baseChance, _factorList)
</li>

<li>($funcBackLink: "Actually... it can wait another night.", "Consider other activities... if you truly think they are more worthwhile.", [{
    <!--lock-->
    ($funcLock: "reading.painting1.evening")
}])</li>
</ol>